<template name="config-menu__audio">
    <head>
    </head>
    <body>
        <form class="config__form">
            <div class="config__wrapper">
                <div class="config-debug">
                    <div class="config-debug__scroll">
                        <div class="config-debug-option" data-if="aud_changed">
                            <label class="config-debug-option__label">
                                <div style="flex: 1 1 0dp; width: 100%; white-space: normal;">Changed settings apply when the game is next launched.</div>
                            </label>
                        </div>
                        <div class="config-debug-option">
                            <label class="config-debug-option__label">
                                <div>Music</div>
                            </label>
                            <div class="config-debug__option-split">
                                <div class="config-debug__option-controls">
                                    <div class="config-debug__select-wrapper">
                                        <div class="config-debug__select-label" data-event-mouseover="show_tip" data-event-mouseout="hide_tip"><div>Background Music</div><div class="config-tip-text">Towns: every area's music is drawn at random from the game's tracks, freshly on each launch. All: the same, plus everything the game starts by name rather than by area - the title screen, battles and bosses, the victory fanfare, the death jingle, the credits, saving - each swapped for a random track for the session. Works with or without the randomizer.</div></div>
                                        <select data-value="aud_music_shuffle" id="aud_music_shuffle_select" style="nav-up: #tab_audio">
                                            <option value="0">Off</option>
                                            <option value="1">Towns</option>
                                            <option value="2">All</option>
                                        </select>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="config-debug__select-wrapper">
                                        <div class="config-debug__select-label" data-event-mouseover="show_tip" data-event-mouseout="hide_tip"><div>Shuffle sound effects</div><div class="config-tip-text">Every one of the game's 70 sound effects becomes a different one, the same swap for the whole session and a new draw on each launch. Menus, footsteps, spells, hits and all. Any sound still going three seconds after it started is cut, so a looping ambience that lands on a common sound cannot run on.</div></div>
                                        <select data-value="aud_sfx_shuffle" id="aud_sfx_shuffle_select">
                                            <option value="0">Off</option>
                                            <option value="1">On</option>
                                        </select>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="config-debug__select-wrapper">
                                        <div class="config-debug__select-label" data-event-mouseover="show_tip" data-event-mouseout="hide_tip"><div>Custom Music</div><div class="config-tip-text">Plays your own music in place of the game's. Every track_NN.seq file in the custom_music folder next to the game replaces track NN for the session (15 is Melrode Monastery, 2 Melrode, 21 Holy Plains, 13 battles). A file is a sequence in the game's own format; tools/mid2cseq.pl in the source makes one from a MIDI. What was loaded is written to custom_music.txt beside the settings.</div></div>
                                        <select data-value="aud_custom_music" id="aud_custom_music_select">
                                            <option value="0">Off</option>
                                            <option value="1">On</option>
                                        </select>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="config-tip"></div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </form>
    </body>
</template>
